L-enrichment remains unresolved in the review."}, {"id": "rxn_009", "name": "Condensed alternative homologation to C6 aminonitrile", "inputs": ["mol_010", "mol_002", "mol_003", "mol_004", "mol_001"], "outputs": ["mol_014"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": ["elemental copper"], "conditions": {"temperature": "300-370K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": "elemental copper", "aqueous": "true", "other": "anoxic cyanosulfidic pool; condensed net representation of an unresolved multistep homologation branch from acetone-derived nitrile chemistry; multiple HCN equivalents may be involved"}, "mechanism": "Net sequence of one or more further cyanide homologations, sulfide activation, Cu-mediated reductive rearrangement, and amination converts the acetone-cyanohydrin manifold to a C6 aminonitrile.", "reasoning": "The curated review states that Patel et al. (2015) identified a parallel hydroxyacetone-derived route to valine passing through 2-amino-4-methylpentanenitrile, but it does not resolve the intervening stepwise chemistry. This reaction is therefore explicitly speculative in microscopic detail. Placing the branch after acetone cyanohydrin is chemically justified because hydroxyacetone first enters the validated acetone chemistry, and acetone cyanohydrin is the first established nitrile-bearing intermediate from which additional homologation is plausible (Patel et al., 2015)."}, {"id": "rxn_010", "name": "Hydrolysis and chain shortening of C6 aminonitrile to valine", "inputs": ["mol_014", "mol_001"], "outputs": ["mol_015"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": null, "conditions": {"temperature": "320-370K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": "true", "other": "hydrating surface pool; apparent chain-shortening accompanies hydrolysis; ammonia byproduct omitted from graph"}, "mechanism": "Net nitrile hydrolysis with concomitant one-carbon loss converts the C6 aminonitrile to the C5 amino acid valine.", "reasoning": "Patel et al. (2015) and the curated review 